The two backends disagree about SysV's SSE class on purpose. The IR backend
passes and returns a single-eightbyte all-float aggregate in xmm0, which is what
the ABI says and what gcc and tcc do; the legacy backend passes every composite
in the integer file, down an address-based path that never reaches a register
class, and is not going to be taught otherwise. Each is right linked against
itself, so the disagreement is only visible here.

Delete this file if the legacy side ever learns the rule - the runner flags a
muted test that starts passing.
